      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While aspirin can have anti-inflammatory properties, it's not typically recommended for muscle strains due to the risk of gastrointestinal bleeding. The American Society of Anesthesiologists advises against the use of aspirin or other NSAIDs in cases where acute sprains and strains are suspected. It's best to stick with ibuprofen for pain and inflammation. Continue to keep your leg elevated, and perhaps consider cold packs instead of aspirin. If you're unable to alleviate the pain or if the swelling doesn't subside, it might be best to reconsider your plans for tomorrow and seek medical advice. With regards to the presentation, ensure you sit or avoid standing for prolonged periods to give your muscles some rest. Your health is important, and prioritizing it now could save you from more significant issues down the road. If something changes, please don't hesitate to consult a medical professional.",
